# The editor's Random Scenario: Battle Size Small; Water Hexes YES; Try Again, then Map OK;
# Balance Equal; the armies placed (their elapsed time stays 0 under a script); Save Scenario
# as RANDTEST; then Quit answered by Esc and by the letter of NO, inside the yorn routine, and
# at last Yes. It checks the saved scenario, made from the script's seed.
#! program cs
#! seed 9
#! files scenarios/RANDTEST.CIV

rule 1 key space

# Random Scenario; Battle Size: Small.
play until 2:O
text r
play until 2:B
digest
text s

# Water Hexes: YES. The map: Try Again, then Map OK (both menus are titled Options).
play until 2:W
digest
text y
play until 2:O
digest
text t
play until 2:W
text y
play until 2:O
digest
text m

# Balance: Equal. The armies are placed; a key ends the pause after them.
play until 2:B
digest
text e
prompt
digest
key space

# Save Scenario: the description and time limit it was given, then the name.
play until 2:O
digest
text s
play until 4
text RANDTEST
key enter

# Quit: Esc; Quit: NO, by its letter; Quit: Yes.
play until 2:O
text q
prompt
key esc
play until 2:O
text q
prompt
text n
play until 2:O
text q
prompt
text y
repeat space
